#!/bin/bash

# Command dispatcher for OpenVPN Data Channel Offload.
# The Makefile is a thin wrapper over this; both work standalone:
#
#   ./run status      make status
#   ./run install     make install
#   ./run test        make test
#   ./run uninstall   make uninstall

set -uo pipefail
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"

usage() {
    cat <<'MSG'
Usage: ./run <command>

  status     Show current state (read-only). Safe to run any time
  install    Build and install the ovpn-dco-v2 DKMS module, load it, and
             make it load at boot
  test       Smoke test: stand up a REAL DCO tunnel between an OpenVPN
             server and client in two throwaway network namespaces, and check
             the data channel is actually offloaded. Non-zero on failure
  test-compose
             The same proof one layer out: both ends as CONTAINERS, via
             docker compose. Proves a container can drive a module it could
             never install. Non-zero on failure
  uninstall  Unload it, stop it loading at boot, remove the package
  help       This message

Both tests REFUSE to run until the module is loaded -- they are acceptance
tests for install, not diagnostics. Use status before installing.

Typical first run:
  ./run status && ./run install && ./run test && ./run test-compose

WHAT THIS IS FOR. openvpn moves every packet across the kernel/userspace
boundary twice in each direction. DCO keeps the TLS control channel in
userspace and moves the encrypted data path into the kernel, which is worth
several times the throughput on a tunnel you actually push data over.

WHY THE OUT-OF-TREE MODULE. openvpn 2.6 -- what 24.04 ships -- speaks only to
ovpn-dco-v2. The in-tree `ovpn` module merged in Linux 6.16 is for openvpn
2.7, which is not packaged for 24.04. So this kernel already carries a DCO
module that nothing installed here can talk to, and the DKMS one is the only
route to DCO until openvpn 2.7 lands.
MSG
}

cmd="${1:-help}"
shift 2>/dev/null || true

case "$cmd" in
    status)    exec "$HERE/scripts/status.sh" "$@" ;;
    install)   exec "$HERE/scripts/install.sh" "$@" ;;
    test)         exec "$HERE/scripts/smoke-test.sh" "$@" ;;
    test-compose) exec "$HERE/scripts/compose-test.sh" "$@" ;;
    uninstall) exec "$HERE/scripts/uninstall.sh" "$@" ;;
    help|-h|--help) usage ;;
    *) echo "Unknown command: $cmd" >&2; echo >&2; usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
